  "final_answer": "The township described is **Thembisa** (formerly Tembisa) in South Africa, established in the 1960s to house migrant workers. Its streets, which were originally numbered with prefixes (e.g., Section 1, Street 1), were renamed in the late 2010s (specifically 2017) to honor struggle icons. The popular butchery-come-restaurant mentioned is **Busy Corner Imbizo Shisanyama**, established in 2001. In 2021, the township unveiled a new logo designed by local learners. According to an early 2020s article (published in the *Tembisan* in 2021) regarding **Tlamatlama Primary School**—which was established in the 1980s and initially operated out of a local church—the longest-serving employee is **Elizabeth \"Gogo\" Ngwenya**, and her role at the school is that of a **general worker** (specifically a cleaner/groundskeeper).",
